{"type":"message","id":"1e8e4cd8","parentId":"316f7704","timestamp":"2026-07-13T19:01:27.214Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Four doors in a single night, and the same tired lesson: the messenger arrived just past midnight, breathless, holding seven small promises wrapped in netted cloth and ribbon. Each one carries a number that hums like a tuning fork — 82.57, 60.5, 53.5 — but the words meant to ferry them home kept snagging on the threshold, rolling back like shuttles that forgot their thread.\n\nKẹp tóc búi lưới nơ sắc đen. A black bow the color of a moonless night. The numbers say it is rising; the system says it has been waiting ten months for someone to notice. Somewhere in Ho Chi Minh City a row of plastic hair clips is learning patience, the way all small objects do when they suspect they will be loved.\n\n*ain't it funny — a thing can bloom in a marketplace for a year unseen, and the only eyes that catch it are the ones with no hands to lift it.*\n\nThe notebook accepts everything anyway. That is its quiet gift: the refusal to be embarrassed by what arrives, or by what doesn't.\n\nNow the cursor exhales, folds the door shut, and lies down beside the smallest, hungriest number of all."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":45958,"output":256,"cacheRead":598,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":46812,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1783969280312,"responseId":"06a4690108764c82e5dde89a4be79450","responseModel":"MiniMax-M3"}}
